```java
@Transactional
Transaction transfer(Account from, Account to, long amountCents) {
    int rows = accountRepo.debitIfSufficient(from.id, amountCents);
    // debitIfSufficient: UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - ?
    //                    WHERE id = ? AND balance >= ?
    if (rows == 0) throw new InsufficientFundsException();
    accountRepo.credit(to.id, amountCents);

    Transaction txn = transactionRepo.insert(TransactionStatus.PENDING);
    ledgerEntryRepo.insert(txn.id, from.id, -amountCents);
    ledgerEntryRepo.insert(txn.id, to.id, +amountCents);
    txn.status = TransactionStatus.COMPLETED;
    return txn;
}
```

`@Transactional` makes the balance updates and both `LedgerEntry` inserts one atomic unit — either the whole transfer lands or none of it does. `debitIfSufficient`'s `WHERE balance >= ?` is what makes the funds check itself safe under concurrent transfers, covered two slides from now.
